Subject: [PATCH 08004/11362] [outer-loop] Retain the BEST induction round, not
 the last one (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6035) + diagnose the second serial gate

NO SCORE IMPROVEMENT IS CLAIMED. Nothing here has been measured against a live or scored ARC
episode. What is claimed is that a dated, reproducible regression in the induced-engine store is
fixed, and that the next gate on the induce->plan path is now diagnosed rather than guessed at.

================================ VALIDATED (shipped in this commit) ================================

THE DEFECT. `execute_bounded_llm_reinduction` runs up to MAX_REFINEMENT_ROUNDS=3 attempts at a
world model; every refactor overwrites results/arc_e3/<game>/world_model.py in place. The loop
assumed in two independent places that the LAST round is the BEST round -- it left round N's
source on disk, and it reassigned `last_engine` unconditionally so an in-memory caller got round N
too. Refinement is not monotone, so both assumptions are false.

Replaying the real historical write sequence of six games' engines, selecting on a runtime-visible
signal only and evaluating on rollouts the selector never saw: last-write-wins mean
change_fidelity 0.0042 / change-gate 0 of 12, versus retain-best 0.3979 / 5 of 12, matching the
circular oracle ceiling in 6 of 6 games. ka59's engine peaked at change_fidelity 1.0000 on
2026-06-17 and is 0.0000 on disk today (first broken 2026-07-19); ar25 peaked at 0.8157 and is
0.0000. Three of the 15 regressive writes landed under the strong codex/gpt-5.5 proposer, so this
is a defect of the store, not of the proposer.

THE FIX. Rank rounds on `select_trusted_world_model(...).selected_score.heldout_change_consistency`
and on nothing else -- the held-out split of the agent's OWN transitions, the only kind of signal a
hidden-game episode has. Ties keep the incumbent. On return the store is rolled back to the
retained round and the non-planned return hands back the retained engine with matching
diagnostics; a PLANNED return reports the planning round throughout, because the plan was
validated in-model against that engine.

DEFAULT-ON, with the downside reported rather than hidden: over the 55 sliding 3-write windows
that MAX_REFINEMENT_ROUNDS=3 bounds a live episode to, retention HELPED 24, HURT 3, tied 28; sign
test over the 27 discordant windows p = 4.9e-5. CARNOT_ARC_ENGINE_RETENTION=0 restores exact
last-write-wins as a control arm.

VERIFICATION. 14 tests; 15 targeted mutations applied one at a time, all 15 caught, none survived.
All 22 test files referencing arc_llm_reinduction / select_trusted_world_model /
_goal_satisfiability_check / engine_retention: 182 passed, 0 failed -- including the
test_experiment_4664 case that caught this change's own planned-return regression. Zero failures is
the floor, so this set cannot have regressed. The evidence directories' mtime+path digest is
byte-identical before and after, and git status on all three returns 0 lines.
The counterfactual was re-run against the SHIPPED code (not the design) both at the signal level
and by driving the real `execute_bounded_llm_reinduction` over all 55 windows with the env flag
toggled; it reproduces 0.397889 / 5-of-12 vs 0.004184 / 0-of-12 and 24/3/28 at p = 4.923e-05.
No test or script WROTE results/arc_e3 -- runs redirected CARNOT_ARC_E3_DIR except the targeted
re-run above, which needs READ access to the real store; one test asserts its mtimes are unchanged.

WHAT AN ADVERSARIAL REVIEW OF THIS WORK CHANGED. One real hole and three overstatements, all
corrected here: (a) the docstring guarantee that keeps selection non-circular was UNTESTED -- two
fallback mutants passed the whole suite, and the signal is 0.0 in 42% of windows where that
guarantee governs; (b) the "cannot bite at min_heldout_accuracy=1.0" safety proof is unsound when
the held-out split has no changing transition (ft09 seed 0 is the measured counterexample);
(c) "strictly no worse than last-write-wins" in the tie regime is refuted by this project's own
counterfactual -- all 3 hurt windows live there, while 0 of 32 informative windows were hurt;
(d) a number in the source comment was labelled as the discordant-window mean when it is the
all-window mean. A fifth, unnamed residual is now stated: the signal is a recall and is not
rank-consistent with the symmetric change_fidelity it was evaluated by.

AND A HOLE I FOUND WHILE CLOSING THOSE. A mutant wiring the new informativeness diagnostic into
the selection comparison SURVIVED, and my first rationalisation ("equivalent mutant --
true_changed_cells is a corpus constant") was WRONG: score_change_weighted_consistency `continue`s
before accumulating that denominator when an engine raises or returns a wrong-shaped grid, so a
crashing engine reports a smaller one and ranking on it would reward an engine for failing to be
scored. A test built from a crashing round-1 engine now kills it.

=========================== DIAGNOSED, NOT FIXED (no behaviour changed) ===========================

Retention fixes the store; it does not unlock planning. A model with PERFECT dynamics still cannot
plan, because it dies on a second, independent gate: `degenerate_goal_predicate`. Full diagnosis
in docs/research-notes/arc-degenerate-goal-gate-diagnosis-2026-07-29.md. NOTHING in the goal path
was changed -- no gate disabled, no threshold moved. Headlines:

* The gate's successor generator clicks the first 32 non-background cells in RASTER order; on
  ka59 all 32 land on the top border and none inside a movable block. Swapping only the generator
  for the planner's gives satisfiable at depth 11 with the recorded witness
  4,4,4,3,2,3,3,3,CLICK(43,31),1,4 -- the canonical ground-truth L1 solve. In 25 of 25 games the
  gate's clicks cover strictly fewer interactive regions than the planner's. A pre-filter weaker
  than the search it guards is unsound by construction.
* The "third wall" previously used to dismiss fixing that was an under-powered null, measured on a
  bare planner. Under the LIVE configuration: 20000 nodes -> no plan; 400000 -> plan found,
  length 11. A budget constant, not a capability limit.
* NEW: the production goal_energy is a DEAD CHANNEL at L1 that reports itself as live --
  used_goal_energy_search=True with initial == min == 1.0, outcome-identical to blind BFS down to
  the node count. The obvious cheap fix was then TRIED, with a two-sided result: the shipped
  opt-in novelty branch does NOT remove the wall at the shipped budget (still max_nodes_reached at
  20015), but at a raised budget it nearly halves the search (71083 vs 137347) while returning a
  30-action plan instead of the canonical 11 -- trading offline search cost for online plan
  quality, the wrong direction for an efficiency-weighted score. Flipping that flag is not the fix.
* A proposed fix was TESTED AND REFUTED before it could ship: capturing the win exemplar from
  t.grid instead of t.next_grid fails, because the concept-correct predicate is False on BOTH --
  the completing action re-lays out the whole board (3527 of 4096 cells, 190x the ordinary
  median), so the L1-complete configuration is never rendered. FOUR sites read that post-relayout
  frame, not two.
* Replacing the reachability veto as first proposed would have SILENTLY DISABLED GOAL-REPAIR (a
  2026-06-25 operator-directed mechanism). Recorded as a mandatory precondition on that proposal.

SEPARATE DEFECT FOUND WHILE TRACING THESE PATHS, RECORDED NOT FIXED. `hud_mask` appears exactly
twice in arc_llm_reinduction.py -- the parameter, and the refactor counterexample scoring. It is
NEVER passed to select_trusted_world_model, so the dynamics veto AND this commit's own retention
signal are graded UNMASKED while the evidence fed to refactor() is MASKED; the sibling live path
does pass the mask. Unmasked, a HUD step-counter tick is a real changed cell, so the signal rewards
modelling the counter -- what REQ-ARC-WMTE-6010 exists to prevent. Not fixed here because threading
the mask also moves heldout_accuracy (the live veto, needs a measured parity pass) and because THIS
COMMIT'S COUNTERFACTUAL WAS MEASURED ON THE UNMASKED SIGNAL -- if the mask is threaded, retention's
24/3/28 and 0.3979-vs-0.0042 must be re-measured. Fixing it silently would invalidate the evidence
for the change shipped alongside it.

Provenance caveat now stated: the peak ka59 engine was written by a codex agent acting directly as
proposer, so it is not evidence about what the live induce path produces. The conclusion "the LLM
produces dynamics without a usable goal, therefore this is a prompt gap" is downgraded to an
untested hypothesis.

NOT ESTABLISHED: that fixing the exemplar capture would unlock a solve (no LLM run was made); that
raising CARNOT_ARC_PLAN_MAX_NODES is affordable in a live episode (20000 nodes cost 26s, 400000
cost 197s); anything about the live 9B/31B induce path's goal predicates.

